From 6f...? Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] cgroup: preserve freezer state when ptrace stop resumes

Backport the ptrace_stop() freezer transition used by the fixed
LineageOS SM7125 Android 17 kernel.

The SM7125 LineageOS 24.0 tree uses cgroup_leave_frozen(false) after
freezable_schedule(). The SM8350 5.4 tree already contains the companion
freezer.c/cgroup.c changes, but still passed true at this callsite.
Keep the task in the freezer signal path when its cgroup is still
freezing, instead of unconditionally dropping the frozen state.

Reference:
  LineageOS/android_kernel_samsung_sm7125
  lineage-24.0 merge: 9968db0a26919c12d35428cbaa5dcbb187ad19e3
  kernel/signal.c: ptrace_stop()

This is intentionally a separate patch from lemonadep.kernel-new.patch.

---
diff --git a/kernel/signal.c b/kernel/signal.c
--- a/kernel/signal.c
+++ b/kernel/signal.c
@@ -2219,7 +2219,7 @@
 		read_unlock(&tasklist_lock);
 		cgroup_enter_frozen();
 		preempt_enable_no_resched();
 		freezable_schedule();
-		cgroup_leave_frozen(true);
+		cgroup_leave_frozen(false);
 	} else {
